       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) would justify going above that. At that dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI bleeding, and hyponatremia, and there's no added benefit shown.\n\nPlease pick one of these:\n\n1. **Enter a standard dose.** Usual dosing is 50\u2013200 mg once daily. Starting doses are 25\u201350 mg, titrated at intervals of at least one week. Tell me the dose you want, for example 200 mg PO daily.\n2. **Enter 400 mg as written.** If you're intentionally ordering a supratherapeutic dose, for example for a specific refractory indication, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. You may also want to check with pharmacy, since they will likely flag it.\n3. **Fix a typo.** If you meant a different dose, such as 40 mg or 100 mg, tell me the correct number."
